== 3. NEGATIVE CONTROLS
  (a) m = 3 stars with alpha_1 + alpha_2 > pi (outside the hypothesis): Xi = |p0|^5 A + |p3|^5 A3 changes sign.
      Since dim Y^1 = 1 there (beta_1 beta_2 != 0) and M = +-Xi/60 on the witness, no star-supported field works at the zero.
      |p3| scale  0.3: D01,D12,D23 = 1.000,1.005,0.264 (>0), D02 = -0.050 (<0: alpha1+alpha2 > pi), Xi in [3.8695e-02, 3.8695e-02]
      |p3| scale  2.0: D01,D12,D23 = 1.000,1.005,1.760 (>0), D02 = -0.050 (<0: alpha1+alpha2 > pi), Xi in [2.4211e-01, 2.4211e-01]
      |p3| scale  6.0: D01,D12,D23 = 1.000,1.005,5.280 (>0), D02 = -0.050 (<0: alpha1+alpha2 > pi), Xi in [-3.4477e+02, -3.4477e+02]
      rigorous sign change of Xi on the segment: True
  (b) C^2-at-z (Argyris-type) subspace of the generic m=3 star: dim = 2, with zero means dim = 0, so Y^1 contains no nonzero C^2-at-z field (second moments: [])
  (c) tampered witness (6 D12 -> 7 D12 in phi_2): C^1 across [0,p1]: False (must be False)
[time] controls: 1.7s

